29:- **R-023 | Field ownership and replay** — fields 2 and 4 belong to the world, fields 1 and 3 to the book; on replay in the same world (part V) world and rating are not re-asked, synopsis and hero are set anew by player's choice. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:100. Status: CANON.
30:- **R-024 | UI анкета full composition (canon 16.10)** — semantic core of 4 fields expanded in UI, each field names its consumer: Заголовок мира (world list name); Описание мира (= core 2); Синопсис (заявка) (= core 1, optional, 1–3 sentences); Пролог (short backstory/opening scene; Паганель path recon works in the prologue p.16); Язык мира (pack choice p.14, first pack = Russian); Режим походов (земля мира): real / fictional / mixed (p.16), chosen explicitly, NOT derived from genres; Жанры: canonical list of ten — фэнтези, научная фантастика, современная проза (Fiction), LitRPG, хоррор, постапокалипсис, исторический, киберпанк, стимпанк, мифология (multi-select; consumer = Паганель genre insert p.16); Правила мира: line-per-rule «name: description» (consumers = world laws overriding the insert p.16); Социальный строй: one of eleven — нет, феодализм, демократия, анархия, теократия, коммунизм, капитализм, социализм, трайбализм, рабовладение, меркантилизм (consumers = пачка п.20 + social graph p.15); Экономические модификаторы: checkboxes золотой стандарт, серебряная экономика, бартер, командная экономика (consumers = economy heritage p.15 + пачка p.20); Магия: system description (consumers = world laws p.16 + resistance-to-foreign p.19); Рождение героя (= core 3): name optional (empty = random), hints (sex, race, origin), starting age; Isekai = replay in same world (past stay stays in world history, world-that-remembers, part V); Цензура 16+/18+ (= core 4; absent in old UI drafts, added at canon alignment 16.10). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:102–117. Status: CANON.
33:- **R-027 | Заявка книги (book application)** — short 1–3 sentence application written by the player (authorship from line one), skippable (book works without it); after several sessions engine proposes one from player patterns (p.10), player approves/edits. Stored as text + meaning vector (:5002, p.8); drift measurable as a number. Three applications: night ковка priority shifts toward заявка; gap «заявка ↔ accumulated book» shown to player in дайджест; finished-book annotation = rework of заявка with actual content. Hard boundary: заявка = selection criterion, not plan; chooses/edits nothing inside chapters; Селектор/Пила never lead to it (Пифия precedent p.17); drift = plot. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:123–129. Status: CANON.
62:- **R-056 | p.13 chapter and book** — chapter = session log without edits (turns, replicas, journal); never generated separately — fixed by fact of play. Time pace always 1:1: world never drifts vs player in play, pauses, or sleep. Time jump only by player declaration in replica («весь день поднимался в гору»); pack time detector returns field «время» with quote (word forms: time units + numerals + prepositions «через»/«спустя», no LLM). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:394–398. Status: CANON.
63:- **R-057 | Jump rules** — up to a day: instant jump (near circle recomputed by jump, far circle lazy in мастерская by fate vectors p.7; replay p.15); circle discrepancies not masked — delivered as lagging news («вести в этом мире действительно идут неделями»). Over a day = workshop order, world state recomputed in pause. Пила doesn't grow on a jump (no replicas = no data); world faces advance their drift (p.19). Jump never empty: way stated briefly and factually (рутина, Челнок — «долго и без событий»), and by jump end (evening/night) world may serve a surprise: Ткач or DB заготовка (Пифия гороскоп p.17); not every jump (else fast-forward becomes an adventure-call button — «предчувствие» precedent). If player doesn't continue, Селектор hints a possible event or seeds a hook into next morning's пробуждение. Quiet stretch = convenient world move: player writes montage, world answers with event (p.19). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:400–402. Status: CANON.
64:- **R-058 | Chapter = game day frame** — from пробуждение to sleep; sleep closes a day of any length. Replica «легли спать» = finale: closes chapter and session; after a long session it's the standard finale and explicit application for the next session. Engine never creates sessions: next session opens only by player arrival; world never initiates contact or starts first; next-day пробуждение pre-forged in мастерская (утро главы below) and served on return. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:404. Status: CANON.
65:- **R-059 | Prose in player's key** — engine generates: player style transferred by example in prompt; стилизация под классика allowed (external model, batch, not live turn); no manual chapter insert needed; chapter interpretation/morals outside engine loop (never formulated or imposed). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:406. Status: CANON.
66:- **R-060 | Editing scope** — редактура only grammar and punctuation; content never manually edited. Log kept unedited as source of truth for checks; the book (publishable chapter version, incl. player typos/punctuation) is what gets edited. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:408. Status: CANON.
67:- **R-061 | Редактор** — external model, batch mode, cheap tariff (built-in pipeline can't pull a 30–40k-token chapter: hours at ~5.6 tok/s; 3B weak in Russian orthography). Chapter cut into scenes of 2–4k tokens; punctuation sheet fixed (dash, «ёлочки», ellipsis). Edit format = MD: Редактор submits edit list (было → стало), never republishes whole text. After text processing Редактор generates chapter summary (5–6 sentences) in section `## Краткое содержание` — one request, one model. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:410. Status: CANON.
68:- **R-062 | Цензор правок — five code rules** — (1) source/result words aligned 1:1, composition and order unchanged; (2) insertion, deletion, reordering of words fully banned; (3) bearing words (proper names, numbers, negations) never edited under any conditions; (4) allowed word edit = orthography (compound/separate/hyphen, stress vowels, obvious typos); prose punctuation free; MD markup (headings, emphasis) inviolable; (5) fact control: after edit Цензор checks world(name).db entities (names, places, items), mismatch = reject. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:412–418. Status: CANON.
69:- **R-063 | Rejected edits** — edit failing Цензор auto-rejected; player sees rejected in book window tab «Правки Цензора». Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:420. Status: CANON.
70:- **R-064 | Repeat rule** — word «wrong» the same way ≥3 times = possibly intentional (name, new concept, slang; e.g. «олдбанский») → not edited; becomes candidate for world lexicon (night-ковка input, p.8-3). If the repeating word has a dictionary neighbor within ≤2 letters → likely systematic typo: word edited but with a line in night дайджест («возможно намеренное»). Word already in world lexicon never edited. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:422. Status: CANON.
71:- **R-065 | Утро главы (game-day opening)** — chapter = game day; opening = session creation, created by player's arrival; 30-s timer works inside the session the player created. Пробуждение pre-forged: ковка of пробуждение queued from first pause after chapter end (p.7); by end of 8-hour window пробуждение surely in DB; served instantly without live generation (live generation = fallback when no pause between chapters). Two opening branches: (1) player writes immediately: replica opens chapter, world instantly answers with forgen пробуждение; while player reads it, deep parse of their replica runs (once per chapter) and engine prepares relevant answer — reading time covers parse+generation, no idle; (2) player passive: 30-s timer after chapter creation = заготовка selection window for passive opening; engine picks fitting DB record (criteria = состав пробуждения) and opens the day itself; player's reply to it = chapter's first replica. Состав пробуждения: 3 last turns of previous chapter, stats, portrait, position; sleep state inherited from bedtime (after drinking — heavy head and late sun; after hard labor — brokenness); landscape and small feeling (ray, cold, damp, sound) by portrait; goal = provoke player answer. No hooks in пробуждение: mood unknown, open threads untouched. Timer only at chapter opening; later pauses normal — world never rushes. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:424–433. Status: CANON.
72:- **R-066 | Deep parse of first replica** — once per chapter (other replicas give mood only, p.6); one cheap LLM call (p.14), not a separate live-turn stage: latency hidden in пробуждение-reading window (branch 1) or answer-assembly window; per-word vectorization already in conveyor (p.9). JSON fields «намерение / план / предчувствие / незакрытая тема», each with quote from player's replica (not retelling); field below confidence threshold ignored. Fields go to Ткач facts and Пифия player card (p.17). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:435. Status: CANON.
73:- **R-067 | After deep parse** — Селектор may submit a hook on an open thread or trigger an event by mood, anxiety, stats, portrait (replica «плохо спал, было предчувствие» raises event weight for the day). Not every предчувствие realizes same day — else «предчувствие» becomes an adventure-call button; big event = workshop order, fires через главу. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:437. Status: CANON.
74:- **R-068 | «Моя книга» window** — modal window, text editor; player opens from menu and sees: Краткое содержание = дайджест of current chapter (5–6 sentences, generated by Редактор after text processing); tabs: Содержание (all chapters list, navigation), Глава (full edited text), Правки Цензора (what Редактор changed, what was rejected), Сырой лог (unedited session log, optional); editor mode: player edits errors in chapter text right in the window. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:439–443. Status: CANON.
75:- **R-069 | Death, finale, replay** — book belongs to player: death and finale decided by player, engine/world not in power over completion. World asks decision once and waits, no rush: accept as book finale / replay / new world. Two replay forms on inherited event sourcing (p.15: replay+snapshots): мир-который-помнит keeps past hero in world history (corpse or legend, ружьё и тайна, p.12); мир-который-забыл resets all — no attempt in history, honest new sheet. Synopsis at replay = player's choice: keep or rewrite. «Предложение, а не принуждение: невыполненный синопсис — трагедия, а трагедия тоже книга». Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:445. Status: CANON.
76:- **R-070 | Эпилог** — practically standalone chapter, written by the player = the only pure-authorship chapter; player marks important/turning moments (scenes, chapters) = author marking of book peaks. Data consumers: оседание priorities (p.10), book assembly (contents + dramatis personae), annotation (заявка rework with actual content — part II block), regression sessions, Пифия prediction calibration (p.17) on following books. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:447. Status: CANON.
119:- **R-110 | Chapter/book blocks (07)** — chapter log as-is; time 1:1 + jump rules; редактура/Цензор per R-060–R-064; «Моя книга» tabs; заявка block (storage text+vector, three uses, boundary); death/replay («Предлагать, не навязывать…» owner wording); эпилог consumers list. Source: DOCS/07-THEATER-AND-WORLD.md:91–137. Status: PLAN.
182:- **R-155 | index.html chat shell** — topbar: memory health pill, branch tag, API/WS status dots, clock, NEW, PROVIDERS, WORLDS, AGENTS, MONITOR, MODELS, CONFIG, SERVER sidebar toggle; quick commands row: /status, /look, /quests, graph link, /help (RU: статус, осмотреть, квесты, помощь) = service commands as prose-addition (canon p.13 note); input textarea; actions CLR / SAVE (session to markdown) / LOAD (saved sessions modal) / BOOK. Sidebar tabs: World (Graph Overview nodes/edges), Char (Current Character), Sys (Service Status API/WS) = canon tabs мир/герой/система. Source: interface/index.html:196–293. Status: UI.
183:- **R-156 | index.html «Моя книга» modal** — BOOK button opens modal (comment cites paradigm p.13): title «My Book», digest strip «Chapter digest — 5–6 sentences, written by the Editor after the chapter text», four tabs: Contents (chapter list and navigation, filled as chapters close), Chapter (textarea, editor mode — player fixes typos directly), Censor edits («Editor changes, applied and rejected: was → became»), Raw log (unedited session log, optional). Matches canon p.13 window. Source: interface/index.html:614–648. Status: UI.
193:- **R-163 | Owner/player roles + book product UI** — owner = DEVELOPER/architect only, zero operational duties («Я ничего не должен делать»); player = separate consumer: mechanics outputs address the PLAYER (answers/style/digest → player); every canon gate names executor (code/model), owner never in loop, owner word = post-factum распоряжение. Book product UI (owner 09.10): modal «Моя книга» = text editor; top = digest (5–6 sentences, editor writes after text); tabs Содержание / Глава / Правки цензора / Сырой лог; player edits errors directly; chapter nav via contents. Source: AGENT-MECHANICS.md:84–86. Status: PLAN.
